@ [canonical_uuid] fc3a2e9e-1fc5-4b04-a867-431c2ab0584f

& [Threats]
  + an invalid upstream receipt or verification can launder unobserved content into a compiled stitch
  + rejected dominated or uncovered candidates can be smuggled into projection by count or identity substitution
  + prefix derivation ordering field rewriting hint generation source promotion or predicate loss can alter meaning
  + provider metadata or rendered output can be overclaimed as prompt delivery inference or execution authority
  + duplicated unknown noncanonical oversized or tampered retained forms can bypass independent correspondence

& [Controls]
  + revalidate and reverify the full upstream triplet before projection and compare every upstream digest count effect and physical-contact account
  + derive exact stitch set only from canonical selected_candidates and compare field-by-field plus deterministic prefix identities
  + compile and verify through the published stitch implementation then independently recompose all downstream bytes and receipt counts
  + strict parsers closed bounds four-file raw-byte rehash zero current effects and explicit nonauthority fail closed

& [Residual]
  + correctness is bounded to exact typed composition under the published RSO and stitch contracts; semantic usefulness and host delivery remain unproved
